-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- India district boundaries: all 641, Census 2011 delineation.
--
-- Source:  DataMeet maps, https://github.com/datameet/maps/tree/master/Districts
-- Licence: CC BY 2.5 IN. Attribution is carried in the table so a report or
--          an export can cite it without anyone remembering to.
--
-- THE NATIONAL TIER
--
-- 641 polygons cover the whole country, which is what makes the map read as
-- India rather than as one pilot city. Wards stay at full precision for the
-- cities running a pilot, because that is the tier where a boundary being
-- wrong changes somebody's route.
--
-- Geometry is simplified to about a kilometre, invisible at the zooms a
-- national choropleth is read at, taking the payload from 28 MB to roughly
-- one. Simplified with PostGIS ST_SimplifyPreserveTopology rather than
-- ogr2ogr's -simplify: the latter quietly destroyed two to three districts
-- outright at every tolerance tried, and losing Bhavnagar and East Kameng
-- without noticing is precisely the kind of silent error this project can
-- least afford.
--
-- `city` holds the state name at this level: it is the region a district
-- belongs to, the way a ward belongs to a city.
--
-- Idempotent. Depends on: ward-density.sql.
-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

begin;

